  "2016 Q1(a)": {"skill":"Differentiating a product with an inverse tangent.","method":"3 marks","moves":["\\(y\\) is two factors multiplied together, and one is an inverse tangent. Which rules?","Set up the product rule: each factor's derivative times the other.","Differentiate \\(\\tan^{-1} 2x\\), using the chain rule for the \\(2x\\).","Write out both terms and simplify."],"marks":[0,1,1,1],"shows":[null,"\\((\\ldots)\\tan^{-1}2x + x(\\ldots)\\)","\\(1 \\cdot \\tan^{-1}2x\\) or \\(x \\cdot \\dfrac{1}{1 + (2x)^2} \\cdot 2\\)",null],"watch":{"at":2,"text":"\\(\\tan^{-1} 2x\\) is the inverse tangent, not \\(\\frac{1}{\\tan 2x}\\)."}},
  "2016 Q1(b)": {"skill":"Differentiating a quotient, and simplifying.","method":"3 marks","moves":["The function is one expression divided by another. Which rule does that need?","Set up the quotient rule with \\((1 + 4x^2)^2\\) as the denominator.","Complete the numerator.","Multiply out the numerator and collect like terms."],"marks":[0,1,1,1],"shows":[null,"\\((-2x)(1 + 4x^2) - \\ldots\\)","\\(\\dfrac{\\ldots(1 - x^2) \\cdot 8x}{(1 + 4x^2)^2}\\)",null],"watch":{"at":3,"text":"Expand and simplify the numerator carefully. An error after a correct answer loses the last mark."}},
